// Title: Detect when login is performed using a specified account (Cloud break glass account)
// Source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/main/Azure%20Active%20Directory/MonitorCloudBreakGlassAccount.md
// Section: Defender XDR
// Author: Bert-JanP
// Description:
// It is best practice to have break glass accounts, which are excluded from all conditional access policies. To monitor all login activities under a specified account, this Detection Rule can be used. If any activity is performed using the specified account, an alert will be generated.

AADSignInEventsBeta
| where AccountDisplayName  == "Input display name of account here"
| project AccountDisplayName,
     Country,
     IPAddress,
     Timestamp,
     Application,
     DeviceName,
     ReportId,
     LogonType,
     SessionId,
     OSPlatform,
     AccountObjectId,
     AccountUpn

// Title: Detect when login is performed using a specified account (Cloud break glass account)
// Source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/main/Azure%20Active%20Directory/MonitorCloudBreakGlassAccount.md
// Section: Sentinel
// Author: Bert-JanP
// Description:
// It is best practice to have break glass accounts, which are excluded from all conditional access policies. To monitor all login activities under a specified account, this Detection Rule can be used. If any activity is performed using the specified account, an alert will be generated.

SigninLogs
| where UserDisplayName  == "Input display name of account here"
| project UserDisplayName,
     Location,
     IPAddress,
     TimeGenerated,
