## Logic App / Sentinel Workbook Desciption 

<img width="302" height="438" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1adbd3be-ad9a-41b2-ae22-a407d60fa801" />


<img width="1240" height="2243" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5e38b076-b271-46d4-aa01-fd9d6bd655d5" />

#### Description
This Logic App is designed to run on a weekly schedule and automatically generate a high-level vulnerability overview from Microsoft Defender data. It executes an Advanced Hunting query via Microsoft Graph, where devices are grouped into broad categories such as Windows servers, Windows clients, Linux, macOS, and network components. Based on these categories, the workflow aggregates key security metrics, including the total number of vulnerabilities, the number of unique CVEs, exploitable CVEs, affected devices, and average CVSS values. The resulting dataset is then sent to Azure Monitor through the Log Ingestion API and stored in a custom stream for further analysis and reporting. After ingestion, the Logic App checks the HTTP response and marks the run as successful only when a 2xx status is returned; otherwise, it records the error details and terminates with a failure status. Authentication for both Microsoft Graph and Azure Monitor is handled through Managed Identity, so no embedded credentials are required.

The Sentinel workbook provides a consolidated view of TVM vulnerability exposure across key device categories (Windows Clients, macOS, Windows Server, Linux Server, Network Components, and Others/Unknown).
At the top, KPI tiles and the detail table show the latest snapshot per category, including total vulnerabilities, unique CVEs, exploitable CVEs, affected devices, average CVSS score, and average vulnerabilities per device.
The trend section then visualizes how vulnerability volume, average severity (CVSS), and exploitable CVEs evolve over the selected time range, enabling quick comparison between categories and helping identify risk concentration, deterioration trends, and prioritization needs for remediation.


